content at 72, 150 and 225 DPI. This checks independently that the Rust
stored-DEFLATE encoder's output is actually decodable at the larger admitted
raster sizes, not merely byte-stable against a candidate PNG golden.

An A4 300-DPI request exceeds the explicit five-million-pixel raster ceiling.
The same black-box regression proves that requesting `--replace` with this
unsupported resolution refuses and leaves the previously accepted 225-DPI
file byte-for-byte unchanged. The existing ruled/grid visual candidates and
default Cargo binary selection tests also still pass.

**Test:**

```sh
node --test \
