## Direct stored-PNG scanline streaming at maximum DPI — 2026-11-11

The native Rust PNG encoder now interleaves each zero-filter scanline with its
RGBA pixels directly into the bounded stored-DEFLATE stream inside the final
PNG IDAT chunk. It allocates neither a full-size filtered raster nor a second
compressed copy of the output, leaving only the RGBA canvas and encoded PNG.
A new exact pixel-length guard refuses mismatched internal raster dimensions;
physical geometry and encoded output budgets remain unchanged.

The checked-in ruled/grid PDF and PNG golden bytes stay identical. An
independent Node PNG decoder validates chunk CRCs, zlib inflation, unfiltered
RGBA transparency, dimensions and physical resolution for A4 at 72, 150 and
225 DPI, and the still-admitted A5 at the maximum 300 DPI. A4 at 300 DPI
continues to refuse the five-million-pixel ceiling without replacing a
reviewed PNG.

Focused Rust tests and all-feature workspace tests also pass. This changes
memory use, not notebook content or physical-print acceptance.
